You Die","src":"charts","grp":"1001 Albums","list_year":null,"rank":582,"year":1986,"note":null,"total":999,"scaruffi":null},{"id":52032266791182,"name":"Scaruffi 1980s","src":"musthear","grp":null,"list_year":null,"rank":717,"year":null,"note":null,"total":877,"scaruffi":null}],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"The artwork for this album prominently features the band standing in front of The Salford Lads' Club on Coronation Street in Manchester. This photo, taken by the band, transformed the club into an alt-rock shrine, despite initial objections from the club itself. The album's artwork appropriation of the club's image caused the club to hire lawyers and state their disapproval, but later they began to embrace their status. \"The Smiths and Bigmouth strikes again from the Queen is Dead, the album featuring artwork that turned The Selford Ladd's Club into an alt-rock shrine.\"","year":1986,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Alt Rock Shrines ｜ From the Archives","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sKHdTSfDd6E"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"The title track of this 1986 album serves as a strong protest against the British monarchy, an institution seen by some as an outmoded symbol of hereditary privilege. The album's stance was highly provocative for its time. \"The Smith's 1986 album, The Queen is Dead.\"","year":1986,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Songs of Protest","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0ARYt4sYT90"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"Released in mid-June 1986, this album is considered the Smiths' masterpiece, despite being born amid controversy and significant problems with their record company, Rough Trade. It marked a huge improvement over \"Meat Is Murder\" in all aspects—musically, lyrically, and performance-wise—and featured a great collection of pop songs filled with wit, satire, emotion, criticism, and carefully crafted self-pity. \"In mid-June 1986, the Smiths released what is considered to be their masterpiece.\"","year":1986,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"What's The Big Deal About The Smiths","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vev8lzfW6Xo"}]}],"book_tracks":[{"id":174755190495914,"artist":"Smiths","artist_id":217386895395983,"title":"The Queen Is Dead","year":1986,"ess":0,"yt":"UL6dq4jm34E","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Pop británico de los ochenta","scene_id":204561151902107,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#uk-guitar-pop","chapters":["Sección 5.11"],"pages":[[1,158,null]]}],"others":[{"id":183882752072448,"type":"album","name":"The Smiths","year":1984,"weight":33},{"id":176266201654425,"type":"song","name":"How Soon Is Now","year":1984,"weight":28},{"id":261641706924901,"type":"album","name":"Meat Is Murder","year":1985,"weight":27},{"id":163523065903015,"type":"album","name":"Strangeways, Here We Come","year":1987,"weight":25},{"id":110865426553469,"type":"song","name":"This Charming Man","year":1983,"weight":25},{"id":78758595471375,"type":"song","name":"Girlfriend in a Coma","year":1987,"weight":19},{"id":13972599637371,"type":"song","name":"Suffer Little Children","year":1984,"weight":19},{"id":196717230109381,"type":"song","name":"Please, Please, Please Let Me Get What I Want","year":1984,"weight":16},{"id":5397016859538,"type":"album","name":"Hatful of Hollow","year":1984,"weight":15},{"id":11188947345078,"type":"song","name":"Hand in Glove","year":1983,"weight":13},{"id":9719438605352,"type":"song","name":"William, It Was Really Nothing","year":1984,"weight":13},{"id":281210326494878,"type":"song","name":"That Joke Isn't Funny Anymore","year":1985,"weight":7}]}